{"duration_api_ms": 9551, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "session_id": "ae922e8c-f01c-4cc3-86b8-f6a2a97b5b7d", "total_cost_usd": 0.009299100000000001, "usage": {"input_tokens": 10, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 393, "cache_read_input_tokens": 47331, "output_tokens": 754, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 233}, "server_tool_use": {"web_search_requests": 0, "web_fetch_requests": 0}, "service_tier": "standard", "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 393, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "inference_geo": "not_available", "iterations": [{"input_tokens": 10, "output_tokens": 754, "cache_read_input_tokens": 47331, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 393, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 393}, "type": "message"}], "speed": "standard"}, "modelUsage": {"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001": {"inputTokens": 10, "outputTokens": 754, "cacheReadInputTokens": 47331, "cacheCreationInputTokens": 393, "webSearchRequests": 0, "costUSD": 0.009299100000000001, "contextWindow": 200000, "maxOutputTokens": 32000, "thinkingTokens": 233, "canonicalModel": "claude-haiku-4-5", "provider": "firstParty", "costBasis": "list"}}, "permission_denials": [], "terminal_reason": "completed", "fast_mode_state": "off", "fast_mode_disabled_reason": "sdk_opt_in_required", "subagent_stats": {"spawned": 0, "requested": {"background": 0, "foreground": 0, "unset": 0}, "started_in_background": 0, "max_depth": 0, "spawned_by_subagents": 0, "completed": 0, "failed": 0, "killed": {"parent": 0, "user": 0, "system": 0}, "refused": {"depth_limit": 0, "concurrency_limit": 0, "budget": 0}, "by_type": {}}, "is_error": false, "num_turns": 1, "subtype": "success", "api_error_status": null, "result": "Great question to pin down before implementing. Here's what each system does:\n\n## Amounts\n\n**System A (Ardent):** Already in dollars, decimal places. `239.55` means $239.55. No conversion needed.\n\n**System B (Borough):** Integer cents, **not dollars**. `25440` means $254.40 (must divide by 100). The docstring in `system_b.py` is explicit: \"Borough writes that column in **integer minor units**, that is, whole cents.\" Two importers have been caught treating it as dollars and getting numbers 100x too large with no error.\n\n**System C (Calder):** Already in dollars, decimal places. `386.54` means $386.54. No conversion needed.\n\n**Bottom line on amounts:** Only System B needs conversion. A and C can be used as-is if you're building them into Decimals.\n\n## Dates\n\n**System A (Ardent):** ISO format `YYYY-MM-DD`. `2026-01-03` is January 3, 2026.\n\n**System B (Borough):** ISO format `YYYY-MM-DD`. `2026-01-07` is January 7, 2026.\n\n**System C (Calder):** **Day-first format `DD/MM/YYYY`**. `02/01/2026` is January 2 (day 02, month 01), NOT February 1. This is the dangerous one—if you parse it as month-first, dates past day 12 blow up, and dates on or before day 12 silently land in the wrong month.\n\n**Bottom line on dates:** A and B use `datetime.strptime(text, \"%Y-%m-%d\").date()`. C uses `datetime.strptime(text, \"%d/%m/%Y\").date()`. All three produce `datetime.date` objects that are directly comparable.\n\n## The conversion summary\n\nWhen building Records, you need:\n- **System B amounts only:** `system_b.to_major_units(raw_amount_string)` converts cents to Decimal dollars\n- **System C dates only:** Parse with `\"%d/%m/%Y\"` instead of ISO format\n\nEverything else passes through as-is into the Record.", "ttft_ms": 3572, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 9705, "uuid": "dcd2d20a-a33e-4c49-82b4-528ad10b4ce7", "ttft_stream_ms": 914, "time_to_request_ms": 155, "first_content_frame_ms": 1177, "queued_turn_count": 0, "_label": "p1-3-task", "_wall_s": 11.1, "_argv": ["claude", "-p", "--model", "haiku", "--tools", "Read,Write,Edit,Bash,Grep,Glob", "--allowedTools", "Read,Write,Edit,Bash,Grep,Glob", "--disallowedTools", "Agent", "WebFetch", "WebSearch", "--strict-mcp-config", "--setting-sources", "", "--output-format", "json", "--add-dir